  {
    "id" : "category_java_codestyle_LocalVariableCouldBeFinal",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Local Variable Could Be Final",
    "description" : "Detects local variables that are assigned only once and could be declared as final.",
    "explanation" : "Since: PMD 2.2\n\nA local variable assigned only once can be declared final.\n\nExample(s):\n```\npublic class Bar {\n    public void foo () {\n    String txtA = \"a\";          // if txtA will not be assigned again it is better to do this:\n    final String txtB = \"b\";\n    }\n}\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 2,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
      {
        "name" : "Java"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "category_java_codestyle_LocalVariableNamingConventions",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Local Variable Naming Conventions",
    "description" : "This rule enforces configurable naming conventions for local variables and other locally-scoped variables in Java code to ensure they match specified regular expressions, typically following standard Java camel case conventions.",
    "explanation" : "Since: PMD 6.6.0\n\nConfigurable naming conventions for local variable declarations and other locally-scoped\n            variables. This rule reports variable declarations which do not match the regex that applies to their\n            specific kind (e.g. final variable, or catch-clause parameter). Each regex can be configured on the PMD configuration file.\nCheck the [PMD documentation](https://pmd.github.io/pmd-7.16.0/pmd_rules_java_codestyle.html#localvariablenamingconventions) for more information.\n\n            By default this rule uses the standard Java naming convention (Camel case).\n\nExample(s):\n```\nclass Foo {\n                void bar() {\n                    int localVariable = 1; // This is in camel case, so it's ok\n                    int local_variable = 1; // This will be reported unless you change the regex\n\n                    final int i_var = 1; // final local variables can be configured separately\n\n                    try {\n                        foo();\n                    } catch (IllegalArgumentException e_illegal) {\n                        // exception block parameters can be configured separately\n                    }\n\n                }\n            }\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
      {
        "name" : "Java"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "category_java_codestyle_LongVariable",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Excessively Long Variable Names",
    "description" : "This rule detects and discourages the use of excessively long variable names in code.",
    "explanation" : "Since: PMD 0.3\n\nFields, formal arguments, or local variable names that are too long can make the code difficult to follow.\n\nExample(s):\n```\npublic class Something {\n    int reallyLongIntName = -3;             // VIOLATION - Field\n    public static void main( String argumentsList[] ) { // VIOLATION - Formal\n        int otherReallyLongName = -5;       // VIOLATION - Local\n        for (int interestingIntIndex = 0;   // VIOLATION - For\n             interestingIntIndex < 10;\n             interestingIntIndex ++ ) {\n    }\n}\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
      {
        "name" : "minimum",
        "default" : "17",
        "description" : "The variable length reporting threshold"
      }
    ],
    "languages" : [
      {
        "name" : "Java"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "category_java_codestyle_MDBAndSessionBeanNamingConvention",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce MDB And Session Bean Naming Convention",
    "description" : "Ensures that classes implementing SessionBean or MessageDrivenBean are suffixed with 'Bean' as per EJB specification.",
    "explanation" : "Since: PMD 4.0\n\nThe EJB Specification states that any MessageDrivenBean or SessionBean should be suffixed by 'Bean'.\n\nExample(s):\n```\npublic class SomeBean implements SessionBean{}                  // proper name\n\npublic class MissingTheProperSuffix implements SessionBean {}   // non-standard name\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
