    "languages" : [
      {
        "name" : "Java"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "category_java_documentation_CommentSize",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "Documentation",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Comment Size Limits",
    "description" : "Checks if non-header comments exceed a specified maximum length.",
    "explanation" : "Since: PMD 5.0\n\nDetermines whether the dimensions of non-header comments found are within the specified limits.\n\nExample(s):\n```\n/**\n*\n*   too many lines!\n*\n*\n*\n*\n*\n*\n*\n*\n*\n*\n*\n*\n*/\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
      {
        "name" : "Java"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "category_java_documentation_UncommentedEmptyConstructor",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "Documentation",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Document Empty Constructor",
    "description" : "This rule enforces that empty constructors should be explicitly commented to indicate intentionality.",
    "explanation" : "Since: PMD 3.4\n\nUncommented Empty Constructor finds instances where a constructor does not\ncontain statements, but there is no comment. By explicitly commenting empty\nconstructors it is easier to distinguish between intentional (commented)\nand unintentional empty constructors.\n\nExample(s):\n```\npublic Foo() {\n  // This constructor is intentionally empty. Nothing special is needed here.\n}\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 2,
    "parameters" : [
      {
        "name" : "ignoreExplicitConstructorInvocation",
        "default" : "false",
        "description" : "Ignore explicit constructor invocation when deciding whether constructor is empty or not"
      }
    ],
    "languages" : [
      {
        "name" : "Java"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "category_java_documentation_UncommentedEmptyMethodBody",
